# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working copy, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `scripts/provision_postgres.sh` is developed on Windows and
# scp'd to a Linux droplet to run. With core.autocrlf=true a fresh checkout gives it
# CRLF line endings, and bash then reads the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r` and
# fails with a "bad interpreter" error that names a file that plainly exists. The
# heredocs in that script would break the same way.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for SQL applied via `psql -f` on the host.
*.sql text eol=lf
